{
  "summary": "The experiment tested combining the best RNA-only configuration (scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool) with image data (resnet50) via concatenation, achieving validation accuracy of 0.6315 and F1 of 0.6068. This suggests multimodal integration may not improve performance compared to the RNA-only baseline (0.6501 accuracy), but the exact impact of image modality remains uncertain due to limited comparative evidence. Further experiments are needed to isolate the role of fusion strategies or image encoder choices."
}

